&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Accentfuncties binnen \text{…}&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Key Derivation Function</title><link>https://tlnd.org/math/key_derivation_function_en/</link><pubDate>Fri, 28 Oct 2016 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://tlnd.org/math/key_derivation_function_en/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="key-derivation-function-kdf"&gt;Key Derivation Function (KDF)&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;h2 id="cryptographic-key-derivation"&gt;Cryptographic Key Derivation&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cryptography | Key Management | Password Security&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A &lt;strong&gt;Key Derivation Function (KDF)&lt;/strong&gt; is a cryptographic algorithm used to derive one or more secret keys from an existing secret value.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This original value may be a master key, password, passphrase, or another form of secret key material.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;KDFs are fundamental components of modern cryptographic systems and are widely used for encryption, authentication, password protection, and secure key management.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Key Derivation Function</title><link>https://tlnd.org/math/key_derivation_function_nl/</link><pubDate>Fri, 28 Oct 2016 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://tlnd.org/math/key_derivation_function_nl/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="key-derivation-function-kdf"&gt;Key Derivation Function (KDF)&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;h2 id="sleutelafleidingsfunctie"&gt;Sleutelafleidingsfunctie&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cryptografie | Sleutelbeheer | Wachtwoordbeveiliging&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Een &lt;strong&gt;sleutelafleidingsfunctie&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;em&gt;Key Derivation Function&lt;/em&gt;, afgekort &lt;strong&gt;KDF&lt;/strong&gt;) is een cryptografisch algoritme waarmee één of meerdere geheime sleutels worden afgeleid uit een bestaande geheime waarde.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Deze oorspronkelijke waarde kan bijvoorbeeld bestaan uit een hoofdsleutel (&lt;em&gt;master key&lt;/em&gt;), een wachtwoord of een wachtwoordzin (&lt;em&gt;passphrase&lt;/em&gt;).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;KDF&amp;rsquo;s vormen een belangrijk onderdeel van moderne cryptografische systemen en worden onder andere gebruikt voor encryptie, authenticatie, wachtwoordbeveiliging en veilig sleutelbeheer.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>KaTeX</title><link>https://tlnd.org/math/KaTeX/</link><pubDate>Sun, 28 Aug 2016 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://tlnd.org/math/KaTeX/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;🇳🇱 &lt;a href="https://tlnd.org/math/KaTeX_nl/"&gt;Lees deze pagina in het Nederlands&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Just a reminder of how to write formulas.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A simple fraction:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-latex" data-lang="latex"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;\frac&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;4+b&lt;span class="nb"&gt;}{&lt;/span&gt;b-2&lt;span class="nb"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;$$\frac{4+b}{b-2}$$&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Aligned lines:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-latex" data-lang="latex"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;\begin&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;aligned&lt;span class="nb"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; a&lt;span class="nb"&gt;_{&lt;/span&gt;ijk&lt;span class="nb"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; = 2 &lt;span class="k"&gt;\\&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;\text&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;because &lt;span class="nb"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;\|&lt;/span&gt;V&lt;span class="nb"&gt;_&lt;/span&gt;1 - V&lt;span class="nb"&gt;_&lt;/span&gt;2&lt;span class="k"&gt;\|&lt;/span&gt; = &lt;span class="k"&gt;\max&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;_{&lt;/span&gt;i &lt;span class="k"&gt;\in&lt;/span&gt; [d]&lt;span class="nb"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; |V&lt;span class="nb"&gt;^&lt;/span&gt;i&lt;span class="nb"&gt;_&lt;/span&gt;1 - V&lt;span class="nb"&gt;^&lt;/span&gt;i&lt;span class="nb"&gt;_&lt;/span&gt;2|
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;\end&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;aligned&lt;span class="nb"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;$$\begin{aligned}
&amp;amp; a_{ijk} = 2 \
&amp;amp; \text{because } |V_1 - V_2| = \max_{i \in [d]} |V^i_1 - V^i_2|
\end{aligned}$$&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Brackets that grow with their content:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-latex" data-lang="latex"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;\left&lt;/span&gt;( &lt;span class="k"&gt;\frac&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;4+b&lt;span class="nb"&gt;}{&lt;/span&gt;b-2&lt;span class="nb"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;\right&lt;/span&gt;)
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;$$\left( \frac{4+b}{b-2} \right)$$&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Inline formulas go between &lt;code&gt;\\(&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;\\)&lt;/code&gt;, for example \( a^2 + b^2 = c^2 \).&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Supported Functions (KaTeX)</title><link>https://tlnd.org/math/KaTeX_function_list/</link><pubDate>Sat, 19 Mar 2016 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://tlnd.org/math/KaTeX_function_list/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;🇳🇱 &lt;a href="https://tlnd.org/math/KaTeX_function_list_nl/"&gt;Lees deze pagina in het Nederlands&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
